From: F <f@f.local>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 11:17:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci): crash-resilient parity suite runner (Windows parity
 green)

The Windows parity job still exited 1 after the four test fixes: bun test
processes intermittently die on Windows in transpiler/GC/teardown under
accumulated load, exiting non-zero with zero test failures (the crash class
documented in the workflow comment). The per-directory segmentation bounded
it but a segment can still crash.

- scripts/parity-suite-runner.sh: per-segment runner that captures each
  segment's output, retries a segment ONCE with a fresh process ONLY when it
  exits non-zero with zero test failures (crash class), fails immediately on
  any real test failure (never masks), prints a failing segment's full
  output, and keeps the executed-files guard.
- cross-platform.yml: the suite step now delegates to the runner.
- Windows segments run with --parallel=2 to reduce worker-process load (the
  documented crash driver).
- test/release/release-workflow.test.ts: updated to assert the runner script
  preserves the single parity authority (platform-parity.ts), not the old
  inline string.
- docs/OWNERSHIP.md: regenerated (152 areas) for the new scripts/ file.
